event-announcement-generator-project-bri.bodyMarkdown:
A campus events team wants a small program that can turn raw event details into a useful registration announcement. You will build it in three cumulative steps, and each step starts from the working result of the one before it.

By the end, your program will:

- store the event name, location, capacity, and registration count;
- calculate how many seats remain;
- decide whether registration is open;
- produce one readable announcement for the event team.

This project uses only ideas you have already practiced in Module 1: values, `const` and `let`, arithmetic, template literals, comparisons, logical operators, and `if/else`.
